## P0 financial correctness

Job publication funding advanced authoritative publication state without checking whether two idempotent wallet-ledger mutations were actually applied:

- partial-wallet creation could persist `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` with a non-zero `walletReservedAmount` after `JOB_PUBLICATION_RESERVE` returned `false`;
- cancellation/expiry could transition a publication to `CANCELLED` after `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` returned `false`.

That can make publication state disagree with the wallet ledger and later settlement/escrow calculations.

## Fix

- require `JOB_PUBLICATION_RESERVE` to report a newly applied debit before persisting the payment-required publication;
- require `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` to report a newly applied restoring credit before cancellation/expiry advances authoritative state;
- fail closed with a conflict on an already-applied/mismatched operation so the surrounding transaction rolls back instead of manufacturing a financial state transition;
- preserve existing operation keys and source-of-funds restoration semantics;
- document the general invariant that domain financial state must not advance when the corresponding idempotent wallet mutation was not applied.

## Regression coverage

Focused tests prove that:

- a reservation-ledger mismatch never persists a payment-required publication;
- a cancellation release mismatch leaves the publication `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` and unpersisted;
- an expiry release mismatch likewise leaves the publication payable and unpersisted.

## Merge gate

Branch was cut from `master` `7c9d6cdd5441d463f888c25affd3d029f334bfe0` after all post-merge #210 workflows on that exact SHA completed successfully. Do not merge unless all relevant checks are green on the exact current PR head, review threads are clear, and `master` is revalidated immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it safely and rerun the exact-head checks. Merge with a merge commit only.
